<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Korea and Japan</p><h1 class="st-title">Lesser Goguryeo</h1><p class="st-meta">699 CE – 820 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A remnant Goguryeo state in Liaodong under Tang suzerainty, ruled by descendants of the last Goguryeo king.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/goguryeo">Goguryeo</a> fell in 668, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang China</a> tried to govern the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaodong">Liaodong</a> region through members of the former royal house. In 699 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/go-deokmu">Go Deokmu</a>, a son of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bojang-of-goguryeo">Bojang</a>, was appointed to govern the Goguryeo population there, and his line developed a semi-independent polity.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Known only from brief mentions in Chinese sources, Lesser <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/goguryeo">Goguryeo</a> was a dependency of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/later-tang">Tang</a> that sent envoys to the Chinese court in the 8th century. Nothing reliable is known of its internal organisation, and some historians question whether it was ever a distinct state.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>It disappears from the records in the early 9th century and is usually thought to have been absorbed by <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/balhae">Balhae</a> under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seon-of-balhae">Seon</a> around 820.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/lesser-goguryeo.jpg" alt="Lesser Goguryeo" width="320" height="480"><figcaption>Image: Samhanin · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Little_Goguryeo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>699 CE – 820 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Go Deokmu</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/china">China</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Little Goguryeo, Xiao Gaojuli</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=760&amp;focus=lesser-goguryeo" aria-label="Lesser Goguryeo on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7395 977 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lesser Goguryeo lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M8115 1035h0M7771 1192h0M8093 871h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7715 1233h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M7715 1233h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day China. <a href="/atlas?year=760&amp;focus=lesser-goguryeo">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
